    {
      "id": "N3-k4nu3RAzBYXbgCMRM8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9390.005787915996,
      "y": 17503.048692718137,
      "width": 976.5020180833744,
      "height": 540,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c04z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 263135235,
      "version": 965,
      "versionNonce": 1303504579,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789895810004,
      "created": 1789895535303,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "If we hit the \"1\", from that we trarverse around it to\nfind all other connected \"1\". \n\nAt every indices, we can see it as a root of a tree.\nTherefor we can either use BFS or DFS for finding\nthe connected element. \n\nIf we successfully implement the core logic, we have to\nsolve a subproblem which is the duplicated visiting.\nSince we start from a \"1\", we find all other \"1\" --> we\nalready check for \"that\" other \"1\" and we might not\nwant to check it again. ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "If we hit the \"1\", from that we trarverse around it to find all other connected \"1\". \n\nAt every indices, we can see it as a root of a tree. Therefor we can either use BFS or DFS for finding the connected element. \n\nIf we successfully implement the core logic, we have to solve a subproblem which is the duplicated visiting. Since we start from a \"1\", we find all other \"1\" --> we already check for \"that\" other \"1\" and we might not want to check it again. ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
