    {
      "id": "UjO0kiYmb-dIWkHIOREuU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10628.941925415773,
      "y": 17987.533834119546,
      "width": 847.0366032524598,
      "height": 630,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c06v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 348265840,
      "version": 873,
      "versionNonce": 421988720,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789961639421,
      "created": 1789960229831,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "nums = [-6,2,3,-4,6,-2,1,2,2], k = 3 -->\n[2,3,6]Sort the array first, we will have\n            [-6,-4,-2,1,2,2,2,3,6] \nAfter sorting, we count the adjacent element,\nwhich will be equivalent since we sorted. The\ncounts will be append into a slice/array, that\narray will hold a pair {val-freq}\n[{-6,1}, {-4,1}, {-2, 1}, {1,1}, {2,3}, {3,-1}, {6,-\n1}]\nSort descreasing again the counts slice \n--> [{2,3},{-6,1}, {-4,1}, {-2, 1}, {1,1}, {3,1},\n{6,1}, ] \nthe result is the counts[i].Val with i in range(0,\nk)",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "nums = [-6,2,3,-4,6,-2,1,2,2], k = 3 --> [2,3,6]Sort the array first, we will have\n            [-6,-4,-2,1,2,2,2,3,6] \nAfter sorting, we count the adjacent element, which will be equivalent since we sorted. The counts will be append into a slice/array, that array will hold a pair {val-freq}\n[{-6,1}, {-4,1}, {-2, 1}, {1,1}, {2,3}, {3,-1}, {6,-1}]\nSort descreasing again the counts slice \n--> [{2,3},{-6,1}, {-4,1}, {-2, 1}, {1,1}, {3,1}, {6,1}, ] \nthe result is the counts[i].Val with i in range(0, k)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YknfL5uEr6zQaVz4eH8lS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11582.738409610607,
      "y": 17987.222281890285,
      "width": 847.0366032524598,
      "height": 855,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c06w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1065284496,
      "version": 1987,
      "versionNonce": 1383783654,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790039120433,
      "created": 1789961112376,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We can use a map for this. which slightly\nbetter. \nWith slices we need to sort two distinguish\ntimes for two slices/arrays\nLet's see an example with map:\n    1. We dont have to sort the nums array .\n    2. for the count, we use an hashmap and\ncheck, if the element is already in the map -->\nincrease the value. If not, create new key\n    3. tracking for the maximum frequency also. \n    4. Initialize another slice/array with length\nof the max freq --> counts := DistributedArray\n. \n\n    5. Iterate throw hashmap -->\ncounts[map.Key] = map.val. Basically we will have\nthis:\n                0   1   2   3   4   5\n        [  [2,3]  [2]  [3]  [4]  [6]]",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We can use a map for this. which slightly better. \nWith slices we need to sort two distinguish times for two slices/arrays\nLet's see an example with map:\n    1. We dont have to sort the nums array .\n    2. for the count, we use an hashmap and check, if the element is already in the map --> increase the value. If not, create new key\n    3. tracking for the maximum frequency also. \n    4. Initialize another slice/array with length of the max freq --> counts := DistributedArray . \n\n    5. Iterate throw hashmap --> counts[map.Key] = map.val. Basically we will have this:\n                0   1   2   3   4   5\n        [  [2,3]  [2]  [3]  [4]  [6]]",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
